The Dock and menu bar are hidden while a Wine window covers a whole screen, so the Dock no longer wakes under a game.

This repository's patch to the Mac driver (version 1), to be offered to WineHQ. It needs nothing from other patches
except 0014's cursorNeedsReapply flag (the hidden cursor set again after the options change); without 0014 that line is
left out and -updateCursor:TRUE alone is called.

-[WineApplicationController updateFullscreenWindows] already finds a visible window of ours on the active Space that
covers a whole screen (WineWindow.fullscreen, outside a full-screen Space), and is already called on activation, on a
Space change, when a window gains or loses that size, and when such a window is shown, hidden, minimized or restored.
It used that only for CaptureDisplaysForFullscreen, which is off by default. Now, while Wine is the active app and
such a window exists, it adds NSApplicationPresentationHideDock | NSApplicationPresentationHideMenuBar to the
application's presentation options, and takes them off when none is left (or when called while inactive). The other
option bits (0013 and 0014's Cursor Location Assistance bit) are kept, the options are assigned only when they
change, and the cursor is set again after a change, as 0014 does for its own bit. AppKit applies presentation
options only while the app is active (NSApplication.h: "in effect for the system when this application is the active
application"), so another app in front has its Dock. Nothing that blocks Cmd-Tab, Mission Control or App Exposé is
set (no DisableProcessSwitching).

Why: Wine's full-screen window sits above the Dock (window level 26 over the Dock's 20) but the Dock stays live under
it. On macOS 27 the Dock sets its arrow cursor each time the pointer touches its edge of the screen, over a game that
hides the cursor: one arrow that stayed 73 s with 0014 v1, and with 0014 v2 (re-applied every 100 ms) still 225
flashes in 75 s of mouse-look, median 61 ms, longest 240 ms, 19% of the time, all at y 917 to 980 of 982 (mavrik S216,
a sampler of the displayed system cursor beside the DirectInput probe). It also stops the Dock from appearing over
games that show their own pointer and scroll at the bottom edge.

Precedent: SDL's Cocoa backend returns NSApplicationPresentationFullScreen | NSApplicationPresentationHideDock |
NSApplicationPresentationHideMenuBar from -window:willUseFullScreenPresentationOptions: for its exclusive full screen
(src/video/cocoa/SDL_cocoawindow.m, SDL2 and SDL3); that is a full-screen Space. For full screen without a Space it
raises the window level only (kCGMainMenuWindowLevel + 1), as Wine does, which leaves the Dock live underneath.

